We need to implement a "Nearby & Global Mosque Discovery" feature in the app using the Google Places API via our backend service.

📌 Objective:
The mobile app will send user coordinates (latitude, longitude), radius, and an optional search keyword. The backend will query Google Places API (and our database), compute distance, and return a clean list of mosques.

🌐 Endpoint:
GET /api/v1/mosques/nearby

📥 Request Query Parameters:
• latitude (required, number) -> e.g. 51.5074
• longitude (required, number) -> e.g. -0.1278
• radius (optional, number in meters, default: 5000) -> e.g. 5000 (5km)
• search (optional, string) -> e.g. "East London Mosque" or city name

⚙️ Backend Logic:
1. If 'search' query is provided:
   Use Google Places Text Search API (`includedType: "mosque"` or `textQuery: "{search} mosque"`).
2. If no 'search' query (nearby mode):
   Use Google Places Nearby Search API (`includedTypes: ["mosque"]`, locationRestriction with circle of radius).
3. Extract Name, Address, Coordinates, Rating, Place ID, Google Maps URL, and Photo URL (via Places Photos API).
4. Calculate distance from user coordinates (in km or miles).
5. (Optional) Merge with our local database mosques if any custom prayer times exist.

